 'lastname': 'Duarte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/438d3f39-fc8b-59fd-8b67-2b90f7edb8c1', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438d3f39-fc8b-59fd-8b67-2b90f7edb8c1'}, {'abstract': 'Forget leisure suits and disco balls. The decade’s economic tumult changed who Americans were as a people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/02/opinion/sunday/inflation-economy-united-states-1970s.html', 'snippet': 'Forget leisure suits and disco balls. The decade’s economic tumult changed who Americans were as a people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In most histories of how Americans became so polarized, the Great Inflation of the 1970s is given short shrift — sometimes no shrift at all. This is wrong. Inflation was as pivotal a factor in our national crackup as Vietnam and Watergate. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/sunday-review/03Tomasky/03Tomasky-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Real Legacy of the 1970s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Real Legacy of the 1970s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-02T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tomasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tomasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/447c558d-baee-5020-8c1a-003ea01b87b6', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/447c558d-baee-5020-8c1a-003ea01b87b6'}, {'abstract': 'African-American women were written out of the history of the woman suffrage movement. As the centennial of the 19th Amendment approaches, it’s time for a new look at the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/02/opinion/sunday/women-voting-19th-amendment-white-supremacy.html', 'snippet': 'African-American women were written out of the history of the woman suffrage movement. As the centennial of the 19th Amendment approaches, it’s time for a new look at the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans are being forced to choose between a cherished lie and a disconcerting truth as they prepare to celebrate the centennial of the 19th Amendment in 2020. The lie holds that the amendment ended a century-long struggle by guaranteeing women the right to vote. The truth is that it barred states from denying voting rights based on gender but “guaranteed” nothing. More than a dozen states had already granted millions of women voting rights before ratification, and millions of other women — particularly African-Americans in the Jim Crow South — remained shut out of the polls for decades afterward.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 693}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 887, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1989, 'width': 1722, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03staples_terrell/03staples_terrell-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Suffrage Movement Sold Out to White Supremacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When the Suffrage Movement Sold Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, SUSAN B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Ella', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglass, Frederick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrison, William Lloyd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Height, Dorothy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shadd Cary, Mary Ann (1823-93)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanton, Elizabeth Cady', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Truth, Sojourner', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wells, Ida B', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-02T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a548f55-1cc3-5f01-b7be-ca84c452c438', 'word_count': 2061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a548f55-1cc3-5f01-b7be-ca84c452c438'}, {'abstract': 'As secretary of homeland security, she signed the memorandum that created the popular program protecting ‘Dreamers.’ Now she’s fighting to save it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/02/opinion/janet-napolitano-on-dacas-enduring-legacy.html', 'snippet': 'As secretary of homeland security, she signed the memorandum that created the popular program protecting ‘Dreamers.’ Now she’s fighting to save it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all his efforts to undo the work of the prior administration, President Trump’s most striking failure has been his attempt to reverse the Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals program — a reprieve from deportation President Barack Obama issued nearly seven years ago to undocumented immigrants who were brought to the United States as children. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 771}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1594, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/02/opinion/02qa1/02qa1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Janet Napolitano on DACA’s Enduring Legacy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Janet Napolitano and DACA’s Enduring Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napolitano, Janet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-02T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cristian Farias', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cristian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farias', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/59cc9f3a-917d-5961-abdc-5dd26b643a46', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59cc9f3a-917d-5961-abdc-5dd26b643a46'}, {'abstract': "How Catholicism's decline increased partisan polarization on abortion.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/02/opinion/sunday/new-york-abortion-catholicism.html', 'snippet': "How Catholicism's decline increased partisan polarization on abortion.", 'lead_paragraph': 'In a sense it’s not surprising that a renewed debate about abortion would begin in New York State, which passed a law last week — since imitated, to more controversy, by Virginia Democrats — ratifying the right to kill human beings in utero in the third trimester.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03douthat/merlin_150069564_441e1937-256c-4a75-a935-ba27ed33c52d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03douthat/merlin_150069564_441e1937-256c-4a75-a935-ba27ed33c52d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03douthat/merlin_150069564_441e1937-256c-4a75-a935-ba27ed33c52d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03douthat/merlin_150069564_441e1937-256c-4a75-a935-ba27ed33c52d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03douthat/03douthat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/sunday/03douthat/03douthat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':