ype_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b861f919-411f-57de-81e2-342861d71870', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b861f919-411f-57de-81e2-342861d71870'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard to know what to say to people in mourning. Say something anyway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/04/opinion/death-grief-condolences.html', 'snippet': 'It’s hard to know what to say to people in mourning. Say something anyway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — When my mother died in 2012, she left behind a huge collection of memorabilia. Not just the usual love letters, family photographs and cherished recipe cards but also random items that almost no one else bothers to save. Parking tickets. Embossed cocktail napkins from the weddings of people I’ve never heard of. An Alabama Power bill from 1972. Things that meant something to her but whose meaning she never explained to me.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/03renklWeb/03renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/03renklWeb/03renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/03renklWeb/03renklWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/03renklWeb/03renklWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/03/opinion/03renklWeb/03renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp