'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-04T17:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Mind', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/245c5a31-a4ec-50ea-a026-e1df74e00b49', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/245c5a31-a4ec-50ea-a026-e1df74e00b49'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of the restaurant Pinch Chinese, in SoHo, uses the toy blocks as chopstick rests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/04/dining/chopstick-rests-legos.html', 'snippet': 'The owner of the restaurant Pinch Chinese, in SoHo, uses the toy blocks as chopstick rests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Raid the toy box to set the table for your Lunar New Year feast. That’s more or less what Sean Tang did. He’s an owner of Pinch Chinese, a welcoming dim sum (and more) restaurant in SoHo where Legos are used as chopstick rests. He’s a Lego fan and was looking for an unexpected detail, and the result, in collaboration with others involved in the restaurant, was an inspired choice: The tiny bumps on the blocks keep the chopsticks from rolling off. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/merlin_150177294_0272d123-9f66-4a41-968a-fcbdccf082bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/merlin_150177294_0272d123-9f66-4a41-968a-fcbdccf082bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/merlin_150177294_0272d123-9f66-4a41-968a-fcbdccf082bc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/merlin_150177294_0272d123-9f66-4a41-968a-fcbdccf082bc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/06burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/06burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner4/06burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Set the Dinner Table With Legos', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Improvise: Restaurant in SoHo Has Some Fun With Legos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chopsticks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-04T17:12:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7839c535-157e-5a2b-aa5e-9f77f40157b6', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7839c535-157e-5a2b-aa5e-9f77f40157b6'}, {'abstract': 'Mix a drink with tequila, crème de cassis and dry sparkling wine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/04/dining/cocktail-valentines-day.html', 'snippet': 'Mix a drink with tequila, crème de cassis and dry sparkling wine.', 'lead_paragraph': "A vibrant cocktail, ruby-red and sparkling, will set the tone for an intimate Valentine’s dinner at home. Called Los Amores and inspired by a Kir Royale, it was created by Patrick Timmis, the beverage director for the Bien Trucha Group, a family-owned Mexican restaurant and catering company in Geneva, Ill., with four places: Bien Trucha, A Toda Madre, Quiubo and Santo Cielo. Muddle two ripe strawberries in a cocktail shaker, add three-fourths ounce each of lime juice and simple syrup, one-quarter ounce of crème de cassis and an ounce of blanco tequila. Shake with ice, strain into a champagne flute, top off with bone-dry sparkling wine and garnish with a strawberry. This makes one drink, but of course you'd prepare enough for two. And consider making more to have refills ready.", 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/merlin_150161616_63ade586-1dd9-4ffc-9664-87bd595fba31-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/merlin_150161616_63ade586-1dd9-4ffc-9664-87bd595fba31-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/merlin_150161616_63ade586-1dd9-4ffc-9664-87bd595fba31-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/merlin_150161616_63ade586-1dd9-4ffc-9664-87bd595fba31-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/06burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/06burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner2/06burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Strawberry Cocktail for Valentine’s Day', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Toast: A Strawberry Cocktail For Valentine’s Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Valentine's Day", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-04T17:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25662c3b-6faf-5b94-b56b-91847aa7c034', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25662c3b-6faf-5b94-b56b-91847aa7c034'}, {'abstract': 'A Belgian chocolate company is offering heart-shaped bonbons in a pink folded envelope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/04/dining/valentines-day-chocolates.html', 'snippet': 'A Belgian chocolate company is offering heart-shaped bonbons in a pink folded envelope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Consider Valentine’s Day as a moment for returning to old-fashioned letter writing and sending. Neuhaus, a Belgian chocolate company, has come up with a delectable Valentine Love Letter gift box for the holiday. The pink folded envelope, sealed with a wax stamp, contains heart-shaped bonbons. There are three varieties, each with an exotic touch: dark and white chocolate with crunchy unrefined sugar and Espelette pepper, milk chocolate with Madagascar vanilla and salted caramel, and white chocolate with raspberry and Yunnan green tea. A flyer in the envelope provides details.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner1/06burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner1/06burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner1/06burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner1/06burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1506, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06burner1/06burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'heig