ubtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06ambriefing-asia-promo/06ambriefing-asia-6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'State of the Union, the Pope, Hummingbirds: Your Wednesday Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T19:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alisha Haridasani Gupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alisha', 'middlename': 'Haridasani', 'lastname': 'Gupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/8893b753-af47-5577-8558-31202875b87d', 'word_count': 1422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8893b753-af47-5577-8558-31202875b87d'}, {'abstract': 'A restaurant in the Africa Center from Pierre Thiam, a branch of Tartinery in Grand Central Terminal and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/dining/nyc-restaurant-news.html', 'snippet': 'A restaurant in the Africa Center from Pierre Thiam, a branch of Tartinery in Grand Central Terminal and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It runs in the family. Cedric Vongerichten, 37, the son of the chef Jean-Georges Vongerichten, has opened a restaurant blending Asia and France, just as his father did. When it comes to Asia, the younger Mr. Vongerichten looks not to Thailand, but to Indonesia, the home country of his wife, Ochi Vongerichten, a partner in the venture. This is his first independent move; he is still the executive chef at the West Village restaurant Perry St., owned by his father’s company. So the name, Wayan, meaning “first-born” in Bali, is fitting. The front of the restaurant has a marble bar, whitewashed brick walls and a few tables. In a passageway to the main dining room in the rear is a shelf with a display of spices used in Indonesian cooking, like long pepper and turmeric root. There’s greenery throughout for a tropical feel, and the design, by Rockwell Group, includes custom Indonesian decorations. Mr. Vongerichten describes the food, most of it served family-style, as coming from a mixture of cultures, using French techniques to interpret Indonesian classics. There’s avocado and a peanut relish instead of spicy peanut sauce on his gado gado, and a rustic cabbage and egg dish; he is using less of the funky shrimp paste that is ubiquitous in Indonesia. Satays, small plates and bright, fruit-forward cocktails are on the menu, but no rijsttafel. (Opens Monday)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06off2/merlin_150060111_15a3a0b7-8a1b-400e-a2f5-a39d440d4582-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06off2/merlin_150060111_15a3a0b7-8a1b-400e-a2f5-a39d440d4582-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06off2/merlin_150060111_15a3a0b7-8a1b-400e-a2f5-a39d440d4582-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06off2/merlin_150060111_15a3a0b7-8a1b-400e-a2f5-a39d440d4582-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/dining/06off