eaturing reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/style/tiny-modern-love-stories.html', 'snippet': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our first night living together, Steve accidentally broke my small colander. It was the first purchase I’d made for my college-bound self the summer after my mother’s suicide. I had coped with her death with a controlled self-sufficiency. Watching that piece of plastic fly out of Steve’s hands and crack on the floor, I felt my fragile facade of security breaking too. But amid my tears, Steve only wanted to understand why a $12 piece of kitchenware was connected to my pain. He isn’t scared to peek into the darkest layers of my life. Steve sees me as my full self. — Elizabeth Jones', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1253, 'width': 1880, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/01/28/fashion/xxtinylove-promo-three2/xxtinylove-promo-three2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Love Stories: ‘Who Are You Sleeping With?’', 'kicker': 'MODERN LOVE', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T20:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da4582e6-a6cf-5f21-ad83-1c85ac2f5e7e', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da4582e6-a6cf-5f21-ad83-1c85ac2f5e7e'}, {'abstract': 'How do you think our country is doing right now? Are we better off than we were a year ago? Why or why not?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/learning/how-would-you-describe-the-state-of-our-union.html', 'snippet': 'How do you think our country is doing right now? Are we better off than we were a year ago? Why or why not?', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump delivered his second State of the Union address on Tuesday night. The speech was scheduled for last month, but was postponed because of the partial government shutdown, prompted by Mr. Trump’s demand that Congress pay for a wall along the southern border with Mexico.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Would YOU Describe the State of Our Union?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T20:28:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Engle and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Engle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05463581-ff85-549e-8ef0-af00f644432b', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05463581-ff85-549e-8ef0-af00f644432b'}, {'abstract': 'The free app doesn’t just help the color-impaired pick out clothes or decode maps — it lets everyone else see through their eyes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-color-blind-pal.html', 'snippet': 'The free app doesn’t just help the color-impaired pick out clothes or decode maps — it lets everyone else see through their eyes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was 12, I became part of the very select group of people who have had a life-changing experience at a fondue restaurant. After repeatedly grabbing my brother’s green fondue fork and eating his steak from the broth pot, I found myself accused of elder-sibling entitlement. But my father, who is colorblind, said I had done nothing wrong; like me, he was unable to see any difference between my brother’s green fork and my orange one. The Ishihara color-vision test he administered on his computer later that night confirmed that I was among those few women with red-green colorblindness. He was excited that I saw “correctly” — which is to say, like him. Back then, the ability to understand his frame of reference was mostly limited to other people barred from becoming astronauts. Now there’s an app for it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1525, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/magazine/10Mag-LOR-1/10Mag-LOR-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Color Blind Pal', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Color Blind Pal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Color Blindness', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon (Ariz)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T20:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zoe Dubno', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zoe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dubno', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bc881e5-ff8d-50e3-9f09-ad5b751d98df', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bc881e5-ff8d-50e3-9f09-ad5b751d98df'}, {'abstract': 'Providing food and medicine will be a key test of the opposition’s push to oust Nicolás Maduro. But aid groups worry about using food as a political tool.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/world/americas/venezuela-humanitarian-aid.html', 'snippet': 'Providing food and medicine will be a key test of the opposition’s push to oust Nicolás Maduro. But aid groups worry about using food as a political tool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — Venezuela’s opposition says it is preparing to deliver tens of millions of dollars in food and medicine to ease devastating shortages and undermine the authoritarian rule of Nicolás Maduro. But some major relief organizations are reluctant to cooperate, fearing the plan could turn humanitarian aid into a political weapon.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/merlin_150234063_98b59921-79c8-4d86-8cbd-7859d73dc7f7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/merlin_150234063_98b59921-79c8-4d86-8cbd-7859d73dc7f7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/merlin_150234063_98b59921-79c8-4d86-8cbd-7859d73dc7f7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/merlin_150234063_98b59921-79c8-4d86-8cbd-7859d73dc7f7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/06venezuelaaid6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/06venezuelaaid6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/world/06venezuelaaid-1-print/06venezuelaaid6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela’s Opposition Plans to Deliver Aid, Undermining Maduro', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Venezuela, Aid With a Political Motive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guaido, Juan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caracas (Venezuela)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T20:37:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anatoly Kurmanaev, Ana Vanessa Herrero and Ernesto Londoño', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anatoly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurmanaev', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ana', 'middlename': 'Vanessa', 'lastname': 'Herrero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Ernesto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Londoño', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fde94941-745c-5622-8925-47795fa428de', 'word_count': 1160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fde94941-745c-5622-8925-47795fa428de'}, {'abstract': 'Three books about presidential speeches and speechwriters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/books/state-of-the-union-books-speeches-speechwriters.html', 'snippet': 'Three books about presidential speeches and speechwriters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, after a one-week delay caused by the government shutdown, President Donald Trump will deliver his second State of the Union address to Congress. He has reportedly been honing its message for weeks with help from Stephen Miller and other members of his communications team, underscoring the central part that speechwriters play in conveying a president’s political ideas. Here are three books that explore this behind-the-scenes role and explain the importance of presidential speeches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1040, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/05/books/05newsbook-presspeeches4/05newsbook-presspeeches4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ahead of the State of the Union, Read About the People Behind the Words', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Thanks, Obama: My Hopey, Changey White House Years (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Litt, David (1986- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'White House Ghosts: Presidents and Their Speechwriters (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schlesinger, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lincoln at Gettysburg: The Words that Remade America (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wills, Garry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T20:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Concepción de León', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Concepción', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de León', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05a7c106-cf20-5748-842a-b8f317a984fe', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05a7c106-cf20-5748-842a-b8f317a984fe'}, {'abstract': 'After a cancellation and before another potential funding lapse, Congress was finally ready to hear what, exactly, the state of the union is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/us/politics/photos-state-of-the-union.html', 'snippet': 'After a cancellation and before another potential funding lapse, Congress was finally ready to hear what, exactly, the state of the union is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They leapt to their feet, dozens of Democratic women, jubilant in their hues of suffragist white as they hugged and grasped hands. For most of the night, they had frequently been stone-faced, often reluctant to applaud President Trump’s declarations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before the State of the Union, a Day of Anticipation and Preparation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Capitol, a Day of Anticipation and Applause', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-05T20:56:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f180892-f168-53d7-996d-3319697c4922', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f180892-f168-53d7-996d-3319697c4922'}, {'abstract': 'Kenyon Victor Adams, a 40-year-old artist and curator, hopes to bring Armstrong’s archive “into the 21st century.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/05/arts/music/louis-armstrong-house-museum-new-director.html', 'snippet': 'Kenyon Victor Adams, a 40-year-old artist and curator, hopes to bring Armstrong’s archive “into the 21st century.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Big changes are coming to the quiet block in Corona, Queens, where Louis Armstrong spent his last three decades. And a new artist and curator has arrived to help guide those changes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times',