rom Sacramento to San Diego. Flash floods have damaged an already fragile landscape, as near hurricane-force winds downed power lines along the coast. On Tuesday, mountain highways were closed because of blizzard conditions and the National Weather Service warned about avalanches in the eastern Sierra Nevada range.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/us/06xp-Ski/merlin_148852158_97189f07-36d7-4f89-b8c4-437bd58bcd8e-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For California’s Ski Resorts, Fierce Storms Are ‘What We Live For’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cross-Country Skiing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Weather Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-06T20:04:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura M. Holson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72b1c17b-6b70-5c46-9952-1b09c6bdd602', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72b1c17b-6b70-5c46-9952-1b09c6bdd602'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/06/books/review/new-releases-edward-st-aubyn-patrick-melrose.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE GOOD IMMIGRANT Edited by Nikesh Shukla and Chimene Suleyman. (Little, Brown, $28.) A wide range of first- and second-generation immigrant writers articulate their feelings of alienation in America during the Trump presidency. Some of the more notable essays include those from Teju Cole, Porochista Khakpour and Alexander Chee. ONLY IN NEW YORK By Sam Roberts. (Empire State Editions, paper, $19.95.) This is an updated edition of Roberts’s collection of eclectic glimpses of New York City. In short bursts of observation he meditates on everything from the city’s highways to Michael Bloomberg’s wealth. JIMMY NEUROSIS By James Oseland. (Ecco, $27.99.) Oseland is a judge on “Top Chef Masters,” but his memoir looks mostly at his pre-culinary days, when he was in a punk band in late-1970s San Francisco and took “Jimmy Neurosis” as his revealing stage name. THE MISSING PAGES By Heghnar Zeitlian Watenpaugh. (Stanford, $30.) This is the biography of a medieval manuscript, the Zeytun Gospels, illuminated by an Armenian artist. When eight pages of that sacred work that had been thought lost were discovered in the J. Paul Getty collection in 2010, a lawsuit ensued. The story of how the pages came to be missing unfolds the entire tragic history of the Armenian people in the 20th century. THE WILD BUNCH By W. K. Stratton. (Bloomsbury, $28.) Sam Peckinpah’s classic western is lovingly picked over in this obsessive treatment of its making and reception.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/books/review/10newnoteworthy0/10newnoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/10/books/review/10newnoteworthy0/10newnoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/books/review/10newnoteworthy0/10newnoteworthy0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/books/rev