es.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The once-divided nature of Berlin isn’t given much consideration in “Berlin, I Love You,” the fifth film in the Cities of Love anthology series. The city itself doesn’t get a whole lot of consideration, either.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1324, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08berlin1/08berlin1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Berlin, I Love You’ Review: Many Stories, Not Much Feeling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Berlin, I Love You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Berlin, I Love You (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Agron, Dianna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knightley, Keira', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luna, Diego', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mirren, Helen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rourke, Mickey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Luke', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-07T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3689d6f6-c0b3-5b73-ab4d-884c089f3fb1', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3689d6f6-c0b3-5b73-ab4d-884c089f3fb1'}, {'abstract': 'Jemima Kirke and Lola Kirke play damaged siblings in this exasperatingly affected romantic drama from Emma Forrest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/07/movies/untogether-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jemima Kirke and Lola Kirke play damaged siblings in this exasperatingly affected romantic drama from Emma Forrest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As far as I can see, the main purpose of “Untogether” is to fetishize Jemima Kirke. Playing Andrea, a writer and barely clean heroin addict, Kirke is a Marilyn Monroe fantasy in vintage frocks and strawberry curls. Stripping, stretching, dancing and posing, she works the camera so assiduously that her latest sexual partner, Nick (Jamie Dornan), barely gets a look in.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 1531, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/06/arts/untogether1/untogether1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Untogether’ Review: Adrift in Los Angeles, Looking for Love', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Untogether', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dornan, Jamie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirke, Jemima', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirke, Lola', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Untogether (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forrest, Emma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-07T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b02ca62-de48-5a3e-b543-c5dd197a991e', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b02ca62-de48-5a3e-b543-c5dd197a991e'}, {'abstract': 'Full of midlife-crisis clichés, the film is yet another ode to the restorative magic of wine country sunshine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/07/movies/under-the-eiffel-tower-review.html', 'snippet': 'Full of midlife-crisis clichés, the film is yet another ode to the restorative magic of wine country sunshine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Under the Eiffel Tower,” Stuart (Matt Walsh), an American bourbon expert fired for a “lack of passion,” likens his existence to the lives of quiet desperation described by Thoreau. “Desperation” seems too mild. When a friend (David Wain) invites Stuart to come along with him, his wife (Michaela Watkins) and their daughter (Dylan Gelula) on a French vacation, the trip has barely started before Stuart proposes marriage to the daughter — who is maybe half his age — at the base of the Eiffel Tower. And that’s before the title card.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/merlin_150234270_61e2888d-9b93-4532-ae93-5c994cfde1f0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/merlin_150234270_61e2888d-9b93-4532-ae93-5c994cfde1f0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/merlin_150234270_61e2888d-9b93-4532-ae93-5c994cfde1f0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/merlin_150234270_61e2888d-9b93-4532-ae93-5c994cfde1f0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/08undertheeiffel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/08undertheeiffel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08undertheeiffel/08undertheeiffel-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Under the Eiffel Tower’ Review: In Whine, Truth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under the Eiffel Tower', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Godreche, Judith', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wain, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Under the Eiffel Tower (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walsh, Matt (1964- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-07T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/74ee062e-7238-5ab6-8a51-70009dbca9d3', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74ee062e-7238-5ab6-8a51-70009dbca9d3'}, {'abstract': 'This haunting documentary guides viewers through heartbreaking tales of the lost souls buried on Hart Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/07/movies/one-million-american-dreams-review.html', 'snippet': 'This haunting documentary guides viewers through heartbreaking tales of the lost souls buried on Hart Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hart Island is in the Pelham Islands group, officially a part of the Bronx. East of the lively City Island, it is a grave site, New York City’s own potter’s field — a term from the New Testament that has come to denote a burial place for the poor, the anonymous, people without family or without family that can afford a marked resting place. The site is managed by the city’s Department of Correction and is not open to the public.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08onemillion/merlin_150222996_05a80863-1e36-44bb-9abc-e33d9aef1ed3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08onemillion/merlin_150222996_05a80863-1e36-44bb-9abc-e33d9aef1ed3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/arts/08onemillion/merlin_150222996_05a80863-1e36-44bb-9abc-e33d9aef1ed3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, '