tname': 'William', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Rashbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/319562f0-959e-509b-8bbb-e3d03dc088a3', 'word_count': 1491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319562f0-959e-509b-8bbb-e3d03dc088a3'}, {'abstract': 'Should we judge people only by their most shameful moments?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/08/opinion/northam-virginia-governor-racism.html', 'snippet': 'Should we judge people only by their most shameful moments?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s probably for the best that Ralph Northam seems determined not to resign as governor of Virginia. He may have done something ugly and dumb many years ago, when he was a young man and prevailing notions of socially permissible behavior were uglier and dumber than they are today. In the face of a political and reputational disaster he has stumbled badly in explaining himself. If he weathers the scandal, it will mainly be because all of his potential successors have grave compromises of their own.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/opinion/08stephensWeb/merlin_150107772_6522f4db-6700-4671-b42f-d64e3c47f620-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/08/opinion/08stephensWeb/merlin_150107772_6522f4db-6700-4671-b42f-d64e3c47f620-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/opinion/08stephensWeb/merlin_150107772_6522f4db-6700-4671-b42f-d64e3c47f620-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None,