ral dozen artists. With Jeffers’s recent public installation, “The Moon, the Earth and Us,” on Manhattan’s High Line, we stopped in to his studio to find out how he makes it all happen. These are edited excerpts from our conversation. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/oakImage-1548700764715-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/oakImage-1548700764715-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/oakImage-1548700764715-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/oakImage-1548700764715-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/12Jeffers99-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/12Jeffers99-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/25/automobiles/25Jeffers-print2/12Jeffers99-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mapping Oliver Jeffers’s World', 'kicker': 'ART OF THE Book', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Artist’s Space: Big on Light (and Leaks)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeffers, Oliver', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'High Line (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Here We Are: Notes for Living on Planet Earth (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Stuck (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-09T10:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maria Russo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd7fe52f-dfef-5dc0-9583-c2a5b6fcb726', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd7fe52f-dfef-5dc0-9583-c2a5b6fcb726'}, {'abstract': 'Vintage photos from the New York Times archive show the enduring power of the pooch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/09/sports/vintage-dog-pictures-instagram.html', 'snippet': 'Vintage photos from the New York Times archive show the enduring power of the pooch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Decades before Instagram or #packwalk, Jim Buck was trouping through the streets of New York with multiple leashes and multiple dogs in tow. In 1964, Gay Talese profiled Buck, pictured above, in The New York Times. “145-Pounder Walks 500 Pounds of Dogs,” ran the headline. That doesn’t sound exceptional now, but Buck was apparently the first professional dog walker. In the story, Talese noted that Buck was 32, married with two children and two big dogs of his own. He was making a decent income — in the low six figures, in today’s dollars — in electronic sales. But, Talese explained, Buck was bored. He loved animals and the outdoors, so, with “a little advertising and a little salesmanship,” he began a dog-walking business and not only earned a living but also became a fixture of the Upper East Side. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1395, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/08/multimedia/08Dogs-AST-17-promo/08Dogs-AST-17-promo-thumbLar