lue': 'National Enquirer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extortion and Blackmail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-09T19:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maureen Dowd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maureen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dowd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/43784a84-6d65-5450-9dbc-1f0fc25b0303', 'word_count': 891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43784a84-6d65-5450-9dbc-1f0fc25b0303'}, {'abstract': 'I don’t want to focus on how rape changed me. I want to focus on changing rape culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/09/opinion/sunday/mythology-rape.html', 'snippet': 'I don’t want to focus on how rape changed me. I want to focus on changing rape culture.', 'lead_paragraph': "Obsessed with mythology as a girl, I read and reread the “Book of Greek Myths,” by Ingri and Edgar Parin d'Aulaire. I fell in love with Artemis — her lack of sentimentality, her plea to Zeus to never have to marry. I even admired her assassination of Actaeon, the man who spied on her as she bathed. She splashed him with  water and turned him into a stag; he was devoured by his own hounds. The book calls her “a cold and pitiless goddess,” but to me she was self-assured, unapologetically powerful.", 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 824}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/sunday-review/10shields/10shields-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Make Me a Cold and Pitiless Goddess', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Make Me a Cold and Pitiless Goddess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Myths and Mythical Creatures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-09T19:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharma Shields', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shields', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/197ff6fa-1f11-5f84-a2e6-a8a46edb1be7', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/197ff6fa-1f11-5f84-a2e6-a8a46edb1be7'}, {'abstract': 'At least our future socialist overlords aren’t thinking small.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/09/opinion/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-green-new-deal.html', 'snippet': 'At least our future socialist overlords aren’t thinking small.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first major policy intervention from Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, the noted social-media personality and future dictator-for-life of the Americas (I believe she’s also a congresswoman of some sort), is a quite-extraordinary document: a blueprint for fighting climate change that manages to confirm every conservative critique of liberal environmental activism, every Republican suspicion of what global-warming alarm is really all about.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/opinion/sunday/10Douthat/merlin_150321585_5ba76a05-e8b4-4e00-b790-23cc67f44ce7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/10/opinion/sunday/10Douthat/merlin_150321585_5ba76a05-e8b4-4e00-b790-23cc67f44ce7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/10/opinion/sunday/10Douthat/merlin_150321585_5ba76