 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/11/obituaries/nancy-b-reich-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Her research raised the profile of a composer too often overshadowed by her husband and established her as a major figure of German Romanticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nancy B. Reich, whose seminal 1985 biography of Clara Schumann established her as an important musical figure independent of her husband, the composer Robert Schumann, and helped turn the musicological spotlight on female composers, died on Jan. 31 in Ossining, N.Y. She was 94.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/obituaries/12REICH1/merlin_150312459_49458666-aaa9-4218-b141-5dab79191526-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/obituaries/12REICH1/merlin_150312459_49458666-aaa9-4218-b141-5dab79191526-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/obituaries/12REICH1/merlin_150312459_49458666-aaa9-4218-b141-5dab79191526-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/obituaries/12REICH1/merlin_150312459_49458666-aaa9-4218-b141-5dab79191526-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1193, 'width': 1473, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/obituaries/12REICH1/08REICH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/12/obituaries/12REICH1/08REICH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thu