e': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/066b3f09-6cfe-5a56-84ba-9095557eb47e', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/066b3f09-6cfe-5a56-84ba-9095557eb47e'}, {'abstract': 'New data for 2018’s fourth quarter shows the British economy growing at its slowest pace since 2012, bringing the broad impact of a no-deal split from the European Union into sharp relief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/11/business/brexit-economy-europe-britain-netherlands.html', 'snippet': 'New data for 2018’s fourth quarter shows the British economy growing at its slowest pace since 2012, bringing the broad impact of a no-deal split from the European Union into sharp relief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMSTERDAM — If anyone in the Netherlands is happy about Britain jilting the European Union, they keep that sentiment to themselves. The country has been built on trade, with huge volumes of goods flowing from its ports across the English Channel. Brexit, as the divorce is known, has proved disruptive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/business/12brexitmess-1-print/merlin_150530043_fb693513-47f1-488e-a212-083acbecf3c9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/business/12brexitmess-1-print/merlin_150530043_fb693513-47f1-488e-a212-083acbecf3c9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/business/12brexitmess-1-print/merlin_150530043_fb693513-47f1-488e-a212-083acbecf3c9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': Non