rganizations', 'value': 'National Enquirer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Northam, Ralph S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocasio-Cortez, Alexandria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pecker, David J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-12T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins and Bret Stephens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b66f49c-4c25-5e82-a089-83bcebcc5aa7', 'word_count': 1818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b66f49c-4c25-5e82-a089-83bcebcc5aa7'}, {'abstract': 'A new study confirms that the polarized debate over voter identification isn’t that important.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/12/opinion/voter-id-study-republicans-democrats.html', 'snippet': 'A new study confirms that the polarized debate over voter identification isn’t that important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Usually when some sententious centrist talks about ending partisan polarization and just coming up with “solutions” based on “data” or “studies” or “expert consensus,” the appropriate response is to roll your eyes — the way people have been eye-rolling lately at Howard Schultz of Starbucks and his apparently substance-free vision for an independent presidential campaign. Usually where you find polarization, you also find some issue of great moment, some important conflict of interests or values, that can’t just be turned over to the smart people to solve because any “solution” would inevitably be a victory for one side and a defeat for the other.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/merlin_146429418_909441bb-48f0-4daa-9e0d-309d5b841420-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/merlin_146429418_909441bb-48f0-4daa-9e0d-309d5b841420-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/merlin_146429418_909441bb-48f0-4daa-9e0d-309d5b841420-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/merlin_146429418_909441bb-48f0-4daa-9e0d-309d5b841420-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/12douthatWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/12douthatWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/opinion/12douthatWeb/12douthatWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Myths of Voter ID', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None,