re rascals. Or escape artists. Or vandals, prone to snacking on cellphones. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1436, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/sports/13baddogs/13baddogs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Westminster Dog Show: When Good Dogs Behave Badly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Westminster Kennel Club Dog Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Westminster Kennel Club', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-12T18:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Whiteside', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Whiteside', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dab166c1-409d-5122-aa6f-ca2006474916', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dab166c1-409d-5122-aa6f-ca2006474916'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/12/books/review/new-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATOMIC MARRIAGE By Curtis Sittenfeld, read by Diane Lane. (Audible.) Sittenfeld, the best-selling author of “Prep” and “Eligible,” has produced an original short story for Audible. It’s the tale of a Hollywood power broker intent on turning an evangelical businessman’s best-selling guide to a happy marriage into a blockbuster romantic comedy. THE STRANGER INSIDE By Laura Benedict, read by Therese Plummer. (Hachette Audio.) Kimber Hannon comes home one day to discover a stranger living in her house and insisting he has a right to be there. “I saw what you did,” he tells her. This thriller from Benedict plumbs our everyday fears. POWER MOVES By Adam Grant, read by the author. (Audible.) Grant wants to understand how the nature of power is changing. Where better to consider the shifts than at the World Economic Forum in Davos, where the “thought leaders” gather? He speaks to a handful of them, including Facebook’s Sheryl Sandberg and the former Google chairman Eric Schmidt. THE FORK, THE WITCH, AND THE WORM By Christopher Paolini, read by Gerard Doyle. (Listening Library.) Three original stories from Alagaësia, the world of Eragon and the Inheritance Cycle, are the latest addition to the hit fantasy series full of dragon adventures. THE LAST DAYS OF AUGUST By Jon Ronson, read by the author. (Audible.) Ronson delves into the 2017 suicide of August Ames, a porn star who killed herself a day after being targeted on Twitter for making a homophobic comment. He unravels a more complex story about her life and death.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/books/review/17NewNoteworthy0/17NewNoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/17/books/review/17NewNoteworthy0/17NewNoteworthy0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/books/review/17NewNoteworthy0/17NewNoteworthy0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/books/review/17NewNoteworthy0/17NewNoteworthy0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1214, 'width': 1821, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/books/review/17NewNoteworthy0/17NewNoteworthy0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/17/books/review/17NewNoteworthy0/17NewNoteworthy0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th