oets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpentry and Carpenters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chernow, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lerner, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-12T21:43:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Felsenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felsenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a3f22be-4348-51b7-9411-6b0074e1d558', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a3f22be-4348-51b7-9411-6b0074e1d558'}, {'abstract': 'A former football player, he spent three decades working for Walt Disney, his father-in-law, and had notable successes — until things turned sour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/12/obituaries/ron-miller-dead.html', 'snippet': 'A former football player, he spent three decades working for Walt Disney, his father-in-law, and had notable successes — until things turned sour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ron Miller, who rose through the ranks of his father-in-law’s entertainment company, Walt Disney Productions, but whose time as chief executive was tumultuous and ended with his ouster, died on Saturday at his home in Napa, Calif. He was 85.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/obituaries/13MILLER1/merlin_150533100_0fcc7848-9f00-404e-b3d8-9f5770db9435-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/13/obituaries/13MILLER1/merlin_150533100_0fcc7848-9f00-404e-b3d8-9f5770db9435-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 622}},