ue': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-12T21:46:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/15dc8135-2ac3-548c-95af-f61edd99fd58', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15dc8135-2ac3-548c-95af-f61edd99fd58'}, {'abstract': 'Set in early 1990s Paris, Christophe Honoré’s new film presents us with a middle-aged, H.I.V.-stricken writer falling, wearily, for a bookish 20-something.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/12/movies/sorry-angel-review.html', 'snippet': 'Set in early 1990s Paris, Christophe Honoré’s new film presents us with a middle-aged, H.I.V.-stricken writer falling, wearily, for a bookish 20-something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At first glance, Jacques Tondelli (Pierre Deladonchamps) seems to enjoy an unmoored, cushy life in early 1990s Paris. And the early 1990s Paris Christophe Honoré evokes in this film looks to be a good place for that.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15sorryangel/merlin_150318702_5efbea05-54ce-41ab-a531-3d723ec21d7a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15sorryangel/merlin_150318702_5efbea05-54ce-41ab-a531-3d723ec21d7a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15sorryangel/merlin_150318702_5efbea05-54ce-41ab-a531-3d723ec21d7a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 553