holars and thinkers who have sought reform and opposed the forces of extremism and patriarchy have been arrested. Many of them face the death penalty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 904, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 904}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1360, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/13/opinion/13alaoudh1/13alaoudh1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Father Faces the Death Penalty. This Is Justice in Saudi Arabia.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shariah (Islamic Law)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed bin Salman (1985- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khashoggi, Jamal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Riyadh (Saudi Arabia)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-13T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abdullah Alaoudh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abdullah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alaoudh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b696d752-46ac-5182-b653-6994a9f86ecf', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b696d752-46ac-5182-b653-6994a9f86ecf'}, {'abstract': 'Encouraging and exploiting division has worked for Trump, as far as his own electoral prospects are concerned. Can he keep it up?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/13/opinion/trump-2020-us-them.html', 'snippet': 'Encouraging and exploiting division has worked for Trump, as far as his own electoral prospects are concerned. Can he keep it up?', 'lead_paragraph': 'However often President Trump strays from his favored political strategy, he faithfully returns to it like a dog to a bone: first, polarize the American electorate along racial, cultural and economic lines, then exploit the schisms that have supplanted the class divisions that were once central to both American and European partisan politics.', 'source':