rganizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-13T17:49:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb170fd2-c14f-505f-a66a-7f12a19ef715', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb170fd2-c14f-505f-a66a-7f12a19ef715'}, {'abstract': 'A stylish animated film about a psychiatrist and a gang of art thieves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/13/movies/ruben-brandt-collector-review.html', 'snippet': 'A stylish animated film about a psychiatrist and a gang of art thieves.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Ruben Brandt, Collector” is a curiosity that wants to be more than that. The conceit is rather ingenious: to use a graphically inventive style of animation to manufacture a caper involving the theft of famous paintings. There are 13 of those, including works by Velázquez, Picasso, Manet and Warhol. The picturesque world they inhabit is a distorted mirror of our own, where people routinely defy gravity and have odd physical characteristics. A third eye. An extra breast. Elongated limbs. Facial features arranged according to approximately Cubist principles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/merlin_150318219_81578de5-cdb6-4f2a-90b8-b8cbc7c7a571-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/merlin_150318219_81578de5-cdb6-4f2a-90b8-b8cbc7c7a571-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/merlin_150318219_81578de5-cdb6-4f2a-90b8-b8cbc7c7a571-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/merlin_150318219_81578de5-cdb6-4f2a-90b8-b8cbc7c7a571-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/15rubenbrandt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/15rubenbrandt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15rubenbrandt/15rubenbrandt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Ruben Brandt, Collector’ Review: Stealing Inspiration From Great Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Inspiration in Stolen Picassos and Manets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ruben Brandt, Collector (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krstic, Milorad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-13T17:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline'