ung minds occupied (and having fun) through a school sabbatical and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/14/arts/children-culture-winter-activities.html', 'snippet': 'Classical concerts, children’s film series and a festival where technology meets art are among the events that can keep young minds occupied (and having fun) through a school sabbatical and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before I had children who required a cultural education, I had planned out a film history curriculum. I thought we might begin, my hypothetical children and I, with silent short subjects, maybe Georges Méliès’s “A Trip to the Moon,” and work our way chronologically through cinema history. After a couple of years, we’d move on to talkies, lingering on Max Fleischer cartoons and Laurel and Hardy’s comic two-reelers, arriving at Technicolor just in time for my student-offspring to see “The Wizard of Oz” around age 7 or 8.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15family-guide-print2/merlin_142232187_3df5cd8d-15c6-4438-a172-c91025f69d26-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15family-guide-print2/merlin_142232187_3df5cd8d-15c6-4438-a172-c91025f69d26-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15family-guide-print2/merlin_142232187_3df5cd8d-15c6-4438-a172-c91025f69d26-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/arts/15family-guide-print2/merlin_142232187_3df5cd8d-15c6-4438-a172-c91025f69d26-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh