ions', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kinsa Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-14T22:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c06cc01-a725-57b6-9cb8-02c22a7ca16d', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c06cc01-a725-57b6-9cb8-02c22a7ca16d'}, {'abstract': 'We sent the designers behind the buzzy New York brand an instant camera and asked them to capture their home-décor-inspired fall 2019 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/14/t-magazine/vaquera-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'We sent the designers behind the buzzy New York brand an instant camera and asked them to capture their home-décor-inspired fall 2019 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since its founding in 2013, the New York-based brand Vaquera has playfully subverted the concept of a finale look — a collection’s final, showstopping ensemble. The designers Patric DiCaprio, Claire Sullivan and Bryn Taubensee have ended their fashion shows with a white floor-sweeping terry-cloth bathrobe (spring 2018) and a bouffant chef’s smock accessorized with a two-foot-tall toque (fall 2017). But this fashion week, the designers presented perhaps their most memorable showstopper yet: a gown (of sorts) which they titled the Big Pretty. A mountain of lilac satin topped by a gift bow the size of a beach ball, it was so wide that it brushed showgoers’ knees on both sides of the runway. The idea was a riff, explains DiCaprio, on an early fashion meme: a series of newspaper cartoons from the 1850s depicting women drowning in excessively large dresses and captioned with a version of “death by crinoline.” The oversize bow, meanwhile, evoked a giant housewarming gift. The designers had been thinking about domesticity, an idea that informed looks in pajama-like stripes and a shiny brocade reminiscent of ’80s-era curtains. They looked, too, at domestic portraits by Tina Barney, whose subjects often seem inseparable from the chintzy décor of their living rooms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 492}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1679, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/14/t-magazine/fashion/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV/Vaquera-polaroids-slide-KPPV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of Vaquera’s Standout Fall Show, in Pictures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vaquera (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiCaprio, Patric', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Claire (Fashion Designer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taubensee, Bryn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-14T23:18:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Newell-Hanson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newell-Hanson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc54bf10-73c2-59c6-a407-5eae04880b8b', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc54bf10-73c2-59c6-a407-5eae04880b8b'}, {'abstract': 'Economists have long criticized tax breaks to corporations; politicians and the public may be starting to share their skepticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/14/upshot/amazon-foxconn-subsidies-critics.html', 'snippet': 'Economists have long criticized tax breaks to corporations; politicians and the public may be starting to share their skepticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In exchange for tens of thousands of tech jobs, cities promised Amazon the moon — and an airport lounge, and naming rights, and a chance to pocket its own employees’ taxes. States offered incentive packages worth $7 billion, $8.5 billion, $9.7 billion, any of which would have set records.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/upshot/15up-subsidies/merlin_150700683_7136b361-9fee-4bc5-a1e0-e6fc66d8671c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/15/upshot/15up-subsidies/merlin_150700683_7136b361-9fee-4bc5-a1e0-e6fc66d8671c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/upshot/15up-subsidies/merlin_150700683_7136b361-9fee-4bc5-a1e0-e6fc66d8671c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/upshot/15up-subsidies/merlin_150700683_7136b361-9fee-4bc5-a1e0-e6fc66d8671c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/15/upshot/15up-subsidies/14up-subsidies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/15/upshot/15up-subsidies/14up-subsidies-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '