ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b60b675-78df-52f1-beaa-d01e8989c7b5', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b60b675-78df-52f1-beaa-d01e8989c7b5'}, {'abstract': 'Improvise in the kitchen this week! Make roasted fish with ginger and soy, a fried egg quesadilla or fettuccine with ricotta and mint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/15/dining/no-recipes-required.html', 'snippet': 'Improvise in the kitchen this week! Make roasted fish with ginger and soy, a fried egg quesadilla or fettuccine with ricotta and mint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hi and welcome to Five Weeknight Dishes. I absolutely have to show you NYT Cooking’s newest baby, born on Tuesday evening and weighing in at 38 adorable meals. It’s “You Don’t Need a Recipe,” a collection of no-recipe recipes drawn from our boss Sam Sifton’s enormously popular newsletter. Each one is a dish you could cook tonight, and all are intended to make the dinner dance more exciting, free-form and delicious, even when you don’t exactly know the moves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/dining/17NORECIPE-FISH-GINGER-SCALLIONS/17NORECIPE-FISH-GINGER-SCALLIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/17/dining/17NORECIPE-FISH-GINGER-SCALLIONS/17NORECIPE-FISH-GINGER-SCALLIONS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/dining/17NORECIPE-FISH-GINGER-SCALLIONS/17NORECIPE-FISH-GINGER-SCALLIONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/dining/17NORECIPE-FI