, 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c13bdf-d10b-589d-9d07-8a9bb4e78090', 'word_count': 2491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75c13bdf-d10b-589d-9d07-8a9bb4e78090'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Warren’s 1974 book, “The Front Runner,” portrayed a positive, open relationship between two men and sold millions of copies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/15/obituaries/patricia-nell-warren-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Warren’s 1974 book, “The Front Runner,” portrayed a positive, open relationship between two men and sold millions of copies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patricia Nell Warren, whose 1974 novel, “The Front Runner,” was one of the first widely popular books to feature an open romantic relationship between two men, becoming a literary touchstone for many, died on Feb. 9 in Santa Monica, Calif. She was 82.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/books/review/17WARREN-OBIT1/merlin_150746337_a0d0a1c4-21dd-4115-be63-c4672b3efeb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/20/books/review/17WARREN-OBIT1/merlin_150746337_a0d0a1c4-21dd-4115-be63-c4672b3efeb2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/books/review/17WARREN-OBIT1/merlin_150746337_a0d0a1c4-21dd-4115-be63-c4672b3efeb2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/books/review/17WARREN-OBIT1/merlin_150746337_a0d0a1c4-21dd-4115-be63-c4672b3efeb2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJ