'uri': 'nyt://article/64254344-67a1-5809-8aec-24994d7ad3e9'}, {'abstract': 'Plus, tax season brings bad news, and the Fed offers more clues about its change of heart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/16/business/the-week-in-business-amazon-warren-buffett.html', 'snippet': 'Plus, tax season brings bad news, and the Fed offers more clues about its change of heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you have Presidents’ Day off? I hope so, and that you’re spending it someplace warm and dry, even if that’s just a nest of pillows your living room. The third week of February is the peak of winter drear, in my opinion, and we could all use a break from the gray skies and interminable drama in Washington. Whether you’re heading into a short workweek or not, here’s what to know when it starts, from the latest on President Trump and the wall to the market outlook from the billionaire investor Warren Buffett, and other business and tech news.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Business: Amazon Breaks Up With New York, and Warren Buffett Takes Stock', 'kicker': 'with interest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'May, Theresa M', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Jerome H', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-16T18:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlotte Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlotte', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e492ea6e-8c5e-5130-9e3f-5ca908d87190', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e492ea6e-8c5e-5130-9e3f-5ca908d87190'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe the Second Wave celibates were on to something.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/16/opinion/sunday/sex-power-feminism.html', 'snippet': 'Maybe the Second Wave celibates were on to something.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “How to Date Men When You Hate Men,” Blythe Roberson’s hilarious new book about that classic straight woman’s paradox of wanting to smooch her systemic oppressor, there’s a description of a situation familiar to many of us: The author likes a guy, but she can’t tell if he likes her back. After months of mixed messages, she realizes her infatuation has had political consequences. “Instead of focusing on the intersectional-socialist-matriarchal revolution,” Ms. Roberson writes, “I’ve been focusing on whether or not what just happened was a date.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/sunday-review/17willisaronowitz/17willisaronowitz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Let Sex Distract You From the Revolution', 'kicker': None, 