rsons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-16T23:28:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill de Blasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Blasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0801d7de-e506-5ba4-8314-92382cdb9bac', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0801d7de-e506-5ba4-8314-92382cdb9bac'}, {'abstract': 'As it did in 2013 in the concussion lawsuit, the league reached a settlement, hoping, probably against hope, for a troublesome issue to go away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/16/sports/football/nfl-kaepernick-concussions-settlements.html', 'snippet': 'As it did in 2013 in the concussion lawsuit, the league reached a settlement, hoping, probably against hope, for a troublesome issue to go away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L. owners worried about a protracted legal fight. They fretted over potentially embarrassing disclosures. They were concerned about further alienating fans and sponsors. So they took the unusual step of reaching a settlement rather than continue to battle an adversary who was viewed in some circles as a victim of the league’s sharp elbows.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/sports/17KaepernickFolo-print/merlin_143032791_5dada3c0-3b87-4556-843c-17d97cec3510-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': 