A Tour, including the United States Open in 1961. He was unassuming in an era dominated by Arnold Palmer, Jack Nicklaus and Gary Player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gene Littler, a quietly outstanding golfer who was known as Gene the Machine for an uncommonly smooth and consistent swing that propelled him to the 1961 United States Open championship, died on Friday in San Diego. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/obituaries/18littler-obit2/merlin_150797334_af73b232-f498-4a2f-a6e5-292cf68efd51-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/18/obituaries/18littler-obit2/merlin_150797334_af73b232-f498-4a2f-a6e5-292cf68efd51-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 536}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/obituaries/18littler-obit2/merlin_150797334_af73b232-f498-4a2f-a6e5-292cf68efd51-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 916, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/obituaries/18littler-obit2/merlin_150797334_af73b232-f498-4a2f-a6e5-292cf68efd51-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1774, 'width': 1984, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/obituaries/18littler-obit2/merlin_150797334_af73b232-f498-4a2f-a6e5-292cf68efd51-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/18/obituaries/18littler-obit2/merlin_150797334_af73b232-f498-4a2f-a6e5-292cf68efd51-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7