2c-92cd-79558f0e2f37'}, {'abstract': 'The third novel in this propulsive, violent series trains a fictional lens on some of today’s most pressing issues, including the opioid crisis and political corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/17/books/review-border-don-winslow.html', 'snippet': 'The third novel in this propulsive, violent series trains a fictional lens on some of today’s most pressing issues, including the opioid crisis and political corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the blows delivered by Don Winslow’s Cartel trilogy, none may be as devastating as the timing of “The Border,” its stunner of a conclusion. Though Winslow cannot have engineered all of this 14 years ago when he started this series, his sweeping new novel concerns subjects that put it right on the culture’s front burner: the Mexican-American border, the handling of migrant children, the opioid crisis and some barely fictionalized claims about how foreign money has bought influence at the highest level of the U.S. government.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/books/18bookwinslow-cover/18bookwinslow1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/18/books/18bookwinslow-cover/18bookwinslow1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 842}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/books/18bookwinslow-cover/18bookwinslow1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 730, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/18/books/18bookwinslow-cover/18bookwinslow1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1618, 'width': 1153, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_na