ean Union without a deal has been often foretold, and in frightening detail — goods stranded for weeks, shortages of medicines, flight of businesses and jobs. The deadline, 11 p.m. London time on March 29, is so close that the civil service has begun advertising for applicants to an “E.U. Exit Emergencies Centre.” Yet Prime Minister Theresa May and her Parliament seem capable only of futile votes whose main effect is to harden positions and bring the precipice closer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 563, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 563}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 905, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 849, 'width': 905, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/17/opinion/17brexit-edt/17brexit-edt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'hei