, but also very sad. I wish I could be in John’s arms now.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1457, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/dining/20Nigella1/20Nigella1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigella Lawson Was Never Just a Domestic Goddess', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nigella, Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawson, Nigella', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'How to Eat: The Pleasures and Principles of Good Food (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-19T10:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Besha Rodell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Besha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rodell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9efb55d-db20-5623-acac-911eb2451f37', 'word_count': 2172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9efb55d-db20-5623-acac-911eb2451f37'}, {'abstract': 'Plans to ship Moscow’s trash to the provinces are aggravating economic unrest. Confidence in Russia’s direction and in President Vladimir V. Putin have dropped.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/19/world/europe/russia-putin-landfill.html', 'snippet': 'Plans to ship Moscow’s trash to the provinces are aggravating economic unrest. Confidence in Russia’s direction and in President Vladimir V. Putin have dropped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'URDOMA, Russia — Russia’s countryside and smaller cities have long been fertile ground for President Vladimir V. Putin and his message of restoring bygone greatness, but even here, there are limits.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/20/world/20russia-putin1-print/merlin_150618957_5bed5834-5103-48c3-99aa-07351b162b8c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/20/world/20russia-putin1-print/merlin_150618957_5bed5834-5103-48c3