ract': 'Men who could get through 40 or more push-ups had 96 percent less risk of heart problems in the next 10 years than those who quit at 10 or fewer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/20/well/move/how-many-push-ups-can-you-do-it-may-be-a-good-predictor-of-heart-health.html', 'snippet': 'Men who could get through 40 or more push-ups had 96 percent less risk of heart problems in the next 10 years than those who quit at 10 or fewer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could push-ups foretell the future and the state of a person’s heart?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Many Push-Ups Can You Do? It May Be a Good Predictor of Heart Health', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good for Pecs, and the Heart, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-20T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e61866b-2b01-5180-ac64-88934e1d4de3', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e61866b-2b01-5180-ac64-88934e1d4de3'}, {'abstract': 'For many a young black man in our polarizing society, coincidence has become a sustained peril. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/20/magazine/poem-hoodie.html', 'snippet': 'For many a young black man in our polarizing society, coincidence has become a sustained peril. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adolescence is fraught with dangers, not the least of which are teenagers’ assumptions of their own immortality — how could anything stop such vibrant corporeal glory? But parents know how swiftly tragedy can strike and how accidental its targets may be. For many a young black man in our polarizing society, coincidence has become a sustained peril. The mother in January Gill O’Neil’s poem can only watch with her ferocious love and bottomless terror as her son plunges down the path that will shape him; a child simply trying to grow up into a man. Selected by Rita Dove', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: HOODIE', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-20T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': "By January Gill O'Neil and Rita Dove", 'person': [{'firstname': 'January', 'middlename': 'Gill', 'lastname': "O'Neil", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dove', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e884a1d2-95da-5edc-8983-af2ce8305431', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e884a1d2-95da-5edc-8983-af2ce8305431'}, {'abstract': 'How many should you have in a home?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/20/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-on-virtual-home-assistants.html', 'snippet': 'How many should you have in a home?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nena writes: My boyfriend loves virtual assistant devices and wants one in all the rooms of our apartment. I’m uncomfortable with them listening to us. How many should be allowed in our home?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N