i': 'nyt://article/9b03e0a6-4ba3-511f-b9db-322ed853a5a2'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Public Library celebrated the foundational texts of the American gay rights movement, and also writers were rewarded with awards for writing at the 71st Annual Writers Guild Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/20/style/stonewall-50-nypl-party.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Public Library celebrated the foundational texts of the American gay rights movement, and also writers were rewarded with awards for writing at the 71st Annual Writers Guild Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I would like to see a Pen-Pal Club initiated?” That was question eleven on confidential survey sent to members of the Mattachine Society, a midcentury gay and lesbian rights group. Reflecting the risk of being openly L.G.B.T. in the 1960s, an anonymous respondent circled “no,” adding, by typewriter: “Could lead to blackmail.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Writers Deserve Respect? Some Say Yes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stonewall Riots (1969)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Rita Mae', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Edmund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-20T14:55:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Widdicombe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Widdicombe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4edffea9-4418-5045-9049-05f49d25c922', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4edffea9-4418-5045-9049-05f49d25c922'}, {'abstract': 'Students choose different Times columnists and analyze their rhetoric as a means of diving deep into issues and exploring a range of perspectives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/20/learning/reader-idea-follow-a-columnist-to-promote-inquiry-and-open-mindedness.html', 'snippet': 'Students choose different Times columnists and analyze their rhetoric as a means of diving deep into issues and exploring a range of perspectives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, in honor of our Sixth Annual Student Editorial Contest, which begins on Thursday, we’re publishing a series of ideas by teachers who work with argument writing in various imaginative ways. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/learning/Costello1LN/Costello1LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/learning/Costello1LN/Costello1LN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/learning/Costello1LN/Costello1LN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/learning/Costello1LN/Costello1LN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/learning/Costello1LN/Costello1LN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/12/learning/Costello1LN/Costello1LN-thumbStandard.j