ur Own ‘Medicare for All’ Plan. Beware: There Are Tough Choices.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-21T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'The Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Frakt and Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frakt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/85937465-fb3b-5674-a872-a592f92015b8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/85937465-fb3b-5674-a872-a592f92015b8'}, {'abstract': 'Cheddar-sesame-cayenne coins that recall the American South — with a little European flair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/21/magazine/shortbread-cheese-crackers-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Cheddar-sesame-cayenne coins that recall the American South — with a little European flair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On my early Prune menus, there were a few items here and there that made many people ask me where in the South I was raised. There was a whole roast suckling pig, and some fried chicken livers with braised lentils. I kept a perpetual batch of pickled tomatoes on the condiments shelf in the walk-in. And for years I ran deviled eggs on the bar-snacks menu. I can see how that would be taken for a Southern nod, but I was actually referencing the big murky jar of pickled eggs kept for blood-sugar emergencies at a shot-and-beer-and-pool-table joint over on East Fifth Street. The bar I frequently tried to wind down in back then.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-articleLarge.png', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-jumbo.png', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/magazine/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V/24mag-eat-slideshow-slide-EF7V-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My French Grandmother’s Shortbread Makes for Shamefully Addictive Cheese Crackers', 'kicker': 'Eat ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My French Grandmother’s Shortbread Makes for Shamefully Addictive Cheese Crackers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prune (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Gabrielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-21T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabrielle Hamilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabrielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb013bee-9004-5691-a609-e19b830510b4', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb013bee-9004-5691-a609-e19b830510b4'}, {'abstract': 'Known for its gorgeous beaches and hippie vibe, this tiny state in western India also offers a fascinating blend of Indian and Portuguese influences that are reflected in its buildings, cuisine and art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/21/travel/what-to-do-in-goa-india.html', 'snippet': 'Known for its gorgeous beaches and hippie vibe, this tiny state in western India also offers a fascinating blend of Indian and Portuguese influences that are reflected in its buildings, cuisine and art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Think of it as India’s happy place: The state of Goa, which occupies a sliver on the country’s western coast, is where residents of Mumbai, Delhi, Bangalore and other cities converge for long weekends and lazy holidays filled with sun, sand and revelry. These days, the beguiling beaches might look like they’ve been colonized by foreign hippies and rave-goers by the thousands, but the region’s European connection dates back centuries. The Portuguese defeated the Adil Shahi dynasty of Bijapur in 1510, beginning a four-and-a-half-century reign — Goa only became part of India in 1961, 14 years after the rest of the country won its independence from Britain. The result of this commingling of cultures is one of the most fascinating pockets of India, defined by a leisurely pace and laid-back attitude. Perhaps there’s no better way to describe the vibe in Goa than “susegaad,” a Konkani term derived from Portuguese that alludes to a sybaritic, contented way of life — or, as the travel show host and Goa resident Mayur Sharma told me, the feeling that you can “sink into life here.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/travel/24Hours-Goa2/merlin_150596094_a26d0227-d906-4bd0-818b-af8d8de4d326-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/24/travel/24Hours-Goa2/merlin_150596094_a26d0227-d906-4bd0-818b-af8d8de4d326-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/travel/24Hours-Goa2/merlin_150596094_a26d0227-d906-4bd0-818b-af8d8de4d326-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/24/travel/24Hours-Goa2/merlin_150596094_a26d0227-d906-4bd0-818b-af8d8de4d326-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'super