rd_count': 1639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034a4b57-01a0-51a9-9950-663655ed0365'}, {'abstract': 'An expedition of conservationists found a living Wallace’s Giant Bee on remote islands in Indonesia. It hadn’t been seen since 1981.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/21/science/giant-bee-wallace.html', 'snippet': 'An expedition of conservationists found a living Wallace’s Giant Bee on remote islands in Indonesia. It hadn’t been seen since 1981.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been 38 years since scientists last spotted the insect known as Wallace’s Giant Bee, a rare species found only in a group of Indonesian islands called the North Moluccas. With a wingspan of 2.5 inches and a body the size of a human thumb, it’s considered the world’s largest bee, and was feared extinct.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/05/science/22TB-GIANTBEE1/merlin_150965649_7ac0032c-f141-4b72-a729-1b810508c2cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/03/05/science/22TB-GIANTBEE1/merlin_150965649_7ac0032c-f141-4b72-a729-1b810508c2cc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/05/science/22TB-GIANTBEE1/merlin_150965649_7ac0032c-f141-4b72-a729-1b810508c2cc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/05/science/22TB-GIANTBEE1/merlin_150965649_7ac0032c-f141-4b72-a729-1b810508c2cc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'