 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-cake/21tmag-cake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-cake/21tmag-cake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-cake/21tmag-cake-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of a 3-D Cherry Layer Cake', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-21T17:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dinara Kasko', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dinara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasko', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/04b1428b-272e-50f6-a68d-819e0ae753f2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/04b1428b-272e-50f6-a68d-819e0ae753f2'}, {'abstract': 'The Ukrainian architect Dinara Kasko makes structures based on algorithmic models — and they just happen to be rendered in mousse and meringue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/21/t-magazine/3d-printed-food-dessert.html', 'snippet': 'The Ukrainian architect Dinara Kasko makes structures based on algorithmic models — and they just happen to be rendered in mousse and meringue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The topology of a Dinara Kasko cake is difficult to explain without discursions into higher math. A Ukrainian architect, Kasko, 30, is drawn to surfaces that are resolutely unflat. Some bulge outward, morphing into a cluster of perfect spheres, like oversize bubbles skimmed off the top of a bath; some sink in concave dips, suggesting valleys of miniature waves — eerie acts of biomimicry. Others rise and fall in a tessellation of triangles with sharp, jewel-like edges, their vertices multiplying. These are speculative structures, based on algorithmic models. They just happen to be rendered in mousse and meringue, destined not to be revered as monuments but eaten.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '49', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/t-magazine/21tmag-kakso/18tmag-kakso-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret Ingredient for These Desserts: A 3-D Printer', 'kicker': 'T Introduces', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dinara Kasko’s Pastry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pastries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-21T18:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81d155a5-a295-5175-a43b-a1bd31713617', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81d155a5-a295-5175-a43b-a1bd31713617'}, {'abstract': 'The fallen Nissan executive is ensnared in a legal system that has a 99 percent conviction rate. Can he get a fair hearing?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/21/opinion/carlos-ghosn-nissan-japan.html', 'snippet': 'The fallen Nissan executive is ensnared in a legal system that has a 99 percent conviction rate. Can he get a fair hearing?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until last Nov. 19, Carlos Ghosn was the stuff of legend — a citizen of Brazil, Lebanon and France who created a global car-making empire uniting Nissan, Mitsubishi and Renault, and who regularly appeared on television and in glossy magazines. Since Nov. 19, Mr. Ghosn has been locked up in a small cell in a Tokyo detention center with a toilet in the corner, endlessly grilled by prosecutors without the right to have his lawyer present. Whatever Mr. Ghosn did or failed to do, this is not how justice is supposed to work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1249, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1249}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 492, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 984, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/21/opinion/21Ghosn-edt/21Ghosn-edt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlos Ghosn Faces Japanese ‘Justice’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carlos Ghosn Faces Japanese ‘Justice’', 'n