markets.html', 'snippet': 'The company is joining a stampede of high profile start-ups heading toward the public markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Pinterest confidentially filed paperwork to go public, according to two people familiar with the decision, joining a stampede of high-profile start-ups heading toward the public markets. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pinterest Is Said to File for I.P.O.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pinterest Is Said to Quietly File for I.P.O., Joining a Stampede', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pinterest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-21T22:38:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erin Griffith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Griffith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/867b4324-17cb-5f1f-8d56-5abd6906ee4d', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/867b4324-17cb-5f1f-8d56-5abd6906ee4d'}, {'abstract': 'A colossal painting, once claimed to depict a Confederate victory, has carried an evolving meaning. Now, a spectacular restoration at the Atlanta History Center unravels its complex tale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/21/arts/design/confederate-monuments-cyclorama-atlanta.html', 'snippet': 'A colossal painting, once claimed to depict a Confederate victory, has carried an evolving meaning. Now, a spectacular restoration at the Atlanta History Center unravels its complex tale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — If you had visited Atlanta in the early 1960s, you would have found drinking fountains labeled “Colored” and “White.” Driving into the city from the airport today you pass signs for Ralph David Abernathy Freeway, Andrew Young International Boulevard, John Lewis Freedom Parkway. As in the country at large, there have been big changes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1334, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/arts/22cyclorama1/22cyclorama1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'sub