lue': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Art Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HB Studio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ice Theater of New York', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckinsale, Kate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huppert, Isabelle', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rameau, Jean-Philippe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-22T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/830d28bb-5583-53a8-8543-278c74ffbb11', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/830d28bb-5583-53a8-8543-278c74ffbb11'}, {'abstract': 'Most often associated with domestic craft, the humble art form makes its return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/22/t-magazine/papier-mache.html', 'snippet': 'Most often associated with domestic craft, the humble art form makes its return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF THE POWER of art lies in the transformation of reality, then no medium more fully embodies radical metamorphosis than papier-mâché. To create beauty from the layering of torn newsprint bathed in a glue of flour and tap water is to align yourself with childhood, domesticity, ancient cultures, protest and trash. It is a salvage or rescue mission, finding a use for the lowliest of products — yesterday’s news. In an age rife with the sleek and the minimal, papier-mâché (“chewed paper” in French), has less-than-mythic associations: It is homey and sloppy, redolent of kindergarten and the corner store. Like clay, papier-mâché is infinitely moldable, but instead of coming straight from the earth, a noble mix of raw minerals, it has lived another life entirely, from tree to pulp to industrial printing press to breakfast table to garbage bin to art, before emerging entirely unrecognizable in sculptural form.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '72', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1322, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/22/t-magazine/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E/22tmag-papiermache-slide-RB0E-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 