omen and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Salon 94 Bowery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buhai, Sophie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-22T22:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3049540d-e9ab-5902-aee9-dec5439e7a95', 'word_count': 1022, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3049540d-e9ab-5902-aee9-dec5439e7a95'}, {'abstract': 'His knee will recover, and the N.B.A. will be getting rid of its “one-and-done” rule, but student-athletes will still come up short.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/22/sports/zion-williamson-duke-ncaa-rules.html', 'snippet': 'His knee will recover, and the N.B.A. will be getting rid of its “one-and-done” rule, but student-athletes will still come up short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Zion Williamson of Duke went down with a severed shoe and a sprained knee 30 seconds into Wednesday night’s showdown with North Carolina, it was bad news for plenty involved. Williamson now has to deal with an injury. Duke had to play its archrival without its best player and duly lost, 88-72. Nike faced questions about its product’s apparent failure.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/23/sports/23oncollege-print/merlin_150973602_2509583c-fed8-4f3c-b820-21793c626fae-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/23/sports/23oncollege-print/merlin_150973602_2509583c-fed8-4f3c-b820-21793c626fae-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/23/sports/23oncolle