': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/25/world/europe/pensions-war-criminals-belgium.html', 'snippet': 'Details about possible payments were found to be exaggerated, misleading or false, but despite the lack of hard evidence, Germany was put on the defensive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — It certainly sounded scandalous: Germany was paying pensions to Belgians for collaborating with the Nazi occupation during World War II. Politicians and news organizations expressed their outrage noisily.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pensions for Nazi Collaborators? Shocking if True (It’s a Big If)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-25T17:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Milan Schreuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Milan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b720ffdc-e405-5b0a-a12f-12d9fa02a447', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b720ffdc-e405-5b0a-a12f-12d9fa02a447'}, {'abstract': 'The tribute to a 1970 documentary about the musical “Company” is part of the third season of IFC’s “Documentary Now!”',