 the De Gustibus Cooking School.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/25/dining/mexican-food-vegan-de-gustibus-cooking-school.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Chris Owens will demonstrate how to make vegan tacos and tamales at the De Gustibus Cooking School.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the classes at the De Gustibus Cooking School — held in a kitchen setting at Macy’s Herald Square — are demonstrations, but there are also hands-on classes and some given in restaurant kitchens. Next month Chris Owens, the former chef de cuisine at Bar Verde and now the director of innovation and product development for Plantmade by Matthew Kenney, will show how Mexican specialties like tacos and tamales can be made vegan. The class includes a tasting paired with wines.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/dining/27BurnerVegan-1/27BurnerVegan-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/27/dining/27BurnerVegan-1/27BurnerVegan-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/dining/27BurnerVegan-1/27BurnerVegan-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/dining/27BurnerVegan-1/27BurnerVegan-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/dining/27BurnerVegan-1/27BurnerVegan-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbSt