nippet': 'President Abdel Fattah el-Sisi dismissed criticism of his human rights record at the end of a summit of Arab and European leaders, who hope to make deals on migration, terrorism and arms sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — President Abdel Fattah el-Sisi of Egypt, whose government has jailed critics, muzzled the independent press and executed nine prisoners in the past week, has never appreciated lectures on human rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/merlin_151237116_c4e6557d-24ee-44ad-ba57-862216a47c3e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/merlin_151237116_c4e6557d-24ee-44ad-ba57-862216a47c3e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/merlin_151237116_c4e6557d-24ee-44ad-ba57-862216a47c3e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/merlin_151237116_c4e6557d-24ee-44ad-ba57-862216a47c3e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/26egypt-eu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/26egypt-eu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/26/world/26egypt-eu1/26egypt-eu1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s el-Sisi Welcomes European Union Leaders, but Not Their Scolding on Rights', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Greets E.U. Leaders but Chafes at Talk of Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdel Fattah el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salman, King of Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-25T22:38:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d2d0a3e-1b1e-577f-a842-b2508183402d', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d2d0a3e-1b1e-577f-a842-b2508183402d'}, {'abstract': 'Rok Hwang channels what he learned as a ready-to-wear designer at Celine into cleverly tailored and expressive clothes for his brand, Rokh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/25/t-magazine/rokh-rok-hwang.html', 'snippet': 'Rok Hwang channels what he learned as a ready-to-wear designer at Celine into cleverly tailored and expressive clothes for his brand, Rokh.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Unbutton that coat — you’ll find another one underneath,” says the Korean-born designer Rok Hwang, 34, as he points to a mannequin wrapped in a dun gabardine trench coat. The piece can be worn as either one layer or two, joined or separated by a set of buttons at each shoulder. Hwang bases many of his designs on this technique, a splicing together of garments that adds functionality while shifting expectations of what a wardrobe staple can, and should, look like. “People describe my design process as a form of deconstruction,” he says, “But actually, I’m reconstructing — I like taking something that already exists and giving it new shape and meaning.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/t-magazine/fashion/rokh-slide-NUMX/rokh-slide-NUMX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/03/03/t-magazine/fashion/rokh-slide-NUMX/rokh-slide-NUMX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/t-magazine/fashion/rokh-slide-NUMX/rokh-slide-NUMX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/t-magazine/fashion/rokh-slide-NUMX/rokh-slide-NUMX-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'