 new full-time co-director, Jordana De La Cruz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life often isn’t easy for small performing arts venues in New York. Even beloved spaces can struggle with the city’s high rents and competition for fund-raising dollars. But Jack, an interdisciplinary performance space in Brooklyn’s Clinton Hill neighborhood, is showing that it is possible to thrive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/28/arts/28jack-item1/28jack-item1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jack Arts Venue Finds a New Home and Some New Leadership', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jack (Brooklyn, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duffy, Alec', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Clinton Hill (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-26T21:45:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Libbey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Libbey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef6ef923-5c95-53f5-8a40-e7da5135c47b', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef6ef923-5c95-53f5-8a40-e7da5135c47b'}, {'abstract': 'A Broadway jack-of-all-trades, Mr. Bramble also collaborated on the book for the 1980s blockbuster “42nd Street” and directed its Broadway revival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/26/obituaries/mark-bramble-dies.html', 'snippet': 'A Broadway jack-of-all-trades, Mr. Bramble also collaborated on the book for the 1980s blockbuster “42nd Street” and directed its Broadway revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Bramble, a Broadway jack-of-all-trades who wrote or co-wrote the books for the hit 1980s musicals “Barnum” and “42nd Street,” both of which earned him Tony nominations, died on Feb. 20 at a hospital in Baltimore. He was 68.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/27/obituaries/2