 and that if one did manage to do so and grab my feet, I would instinctively grab onto him, and we would both be dragged into death’s maw. His position hasn’t changed. Do I have to do it?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge John Hodgman on Sharks in the Tub', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bonus Advice From Judge John Hodgman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathing and Showering', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-28T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hodgman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodgman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a61fdae7-72b7-5a7b-80f6-34a97f0476c3', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a61fdae7-72b7-5a7b-80f6-34a97f0476c3'}, {'abstract': 'A ballad to yearning and mortality, as biting as ice, as inscrutable as the snowy woods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/02/28/magazine/poem-frost-on-fire.html', 'snippet': 'A ballad to yearning and mortality, as biting as ice, as inscrutable as the snowy woods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'True to its mischievous title, Dean Rader’s book “Self Portrait as Wikipedia Entry” is an eclectic assemblage of tributes and allegories, letters and instructional headers, interspersed with subversive self-portraits. In this poem, even unlikely end words like “a” and “the” turn out to be faithful to the rhyme scheme — a clear homage to Robert Frost, who was known for setting colloquial expressions to classic meter. Frost’s spirit permeates this wintry scene, where each paradox melts into the next. A ballad to yearning and mortality, as biting as ice, as inscrutable as the snowy woods. Selected by Rita Dove', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 234, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 234}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 800, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/03/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Frost on Fire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frost, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-02-28T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Rader and Rita Dove', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rader', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dove', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'rol